  "description": "Phase 4 skeleton golden set per cost_watch.spec.md §7. Covers the threshold ladder (50/75/90/95/100/110), the kill-switch invariant (never fire below 100%), the $0-budget free-tier edge case (spec §8 #3), the no-budget-row fallback (spec §6 'default to $50/day'), the previous_crossings dedupe semantics, the BQ-stale `blind` propagation, and the >3× baseline anomaly hint. Rule-based agent (no LLM) — final_response is the canonical evaluate_cost_watch() output for each user_content input. The harness asserts byte-for-byte equality of crossings + action + percent + blind. Eval criteria per spec §7: false_negative_rate = 0 (any T ≤ percent must appear), kill_switch_accuracy = 1.00 (no over_limit_block below 100%), time_to_alert ≤ 5s (single-function call, measured upstream).",
